{"nodes":[
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_com_swap_commodity_swap","label":"Commodity Swap","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/com_swap.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_com_swaption_commodity_swaption","label":"Commodity Swaption","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/com_swaption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Floating leg (referencing futures settlement or spot prices) is approximated by a lognormal random variable matched to its first two moments (Black-76 style), avoiding full Monte Carlo simulation while capturing correlation between multiple future/spot price observations via an exponential correlation parameterisation."},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_com_varianceswap_commodity_variance_swap","label":"Commodity Variance/Volatility Swap","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/com_varianceswap.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_convertiblebond_convertible_bond","label":"Convertible Bond","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/convertiblebond.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Priced via the Andersen-Buffum jump-diffusion model so that a single local default intensity h(t,S) tied inversely to the stock price links the equity process to the reference credit, allowing joint calibration to both a market default curve and an equity volatility surface via a Fokker-Planck PDE bootstrap; the p=0 case gives a fast simplified calibration."},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_cr_bgs_balance_guaranteed_swap","label":"Balance Guaranteed Swap (BGS)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/cr_bgs.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"BGS is approximated with an auxiliary Flexi Swap whose notional schedule brackets zero-CPR and Max-CPR prepayment scenarios, because a Flexi Swap's optionality over notional redemption paths provides a realistic tradable proxy hedge for the uncertain amortisation of the referenced security."},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_cr_cbo_collateralized_bond_obligation","label":"Collateralized Bond Obligation (CBO)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/cr_cbo.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_cr_cdo_synthetic_cdo","label":"Synthetic CDO","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/cr_cdo.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Tranche losses are modelled with a one-factor Gaussian copula (with an optional stochastic-recovery extension) because it reproduces market-quoted base correlations on index tranches (iTraxx/CDX) while remaining numerically tractable via the Hull-White bucketing algorithm; a flat survival-probability adjustment factor (Forward Default Probability Multiplier) is used to reconcile intrinsic index valuation with quoted index spreads."},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_cr_cds_credit_default_swap","label":"Credit Default Swap (CDS)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/cr_cds.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"A mid-point approximation (default assumed to occur halfway through a premium period) is used so that accrued premium and discounting of contingent payments can be computed in closed form; the model distinguishes the ISDA Real (Composite) Recovery Rate used for curve building/pricing from the Assumed (standard matrix) Recovery Rate used only for spread/upfront conversion."},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_cr_cds_asset_backed_credit_default_swap","label":"Asset Backed Credit Default Swap (ABCDS)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/cr_cds.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_cr_cds_index_credit_default_swap","label":"Index Credit Default Swap","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/cr_cds.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_cr_cdsoption_cds_option","label":"CDS Option","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/cr_cdsoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_cr_indexcdsoption_index_cds_option","label":"Index CDS Option","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/cr_indexcdsoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"A numerical-integration engine is offered alongside the simpler Black-Formula engine because it avoids the Black engine's approximations (deterministic FEP-adjusted forward spread, no price-to-spread strike conversion, no default adjustment when reading market vol) and is therefore considered more accurate, at the cost of a Simpson-rule integration over the FEP-adjusted forward spread distribution."},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_cr_rpa_risk_participation_agreement","label":"Risk Participation Agreement (RPA)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/cr_rpa.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"The protection leg pricing method is chosen by underlying trade structure: vanilla swaps use a fast analytic European-swaption representation of the EPE profile (matching NPV/Delta/Gamma in an LGM1F model), cross-currency swaps use an analytic FX-option representation, while structured/callable/treasury-lock underlyings require a full numeric LGM exposure simulation because their EPE profiles cannot be matched by a single vanilla option proxy."},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_creditlinkedswap_credit_linked_swap","label":"Credit Linked Swap","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/creditlinkedswap.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_curves_curve_building","label":"Curve Building (Curves Overview)","file_type":"document","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/curves.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_doubledigitaloption_double_digital_option","label":"Double Digital Option","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/doubledigitaloption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_accumulator_equity_accumulator","label":"Equity Accumulator","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_accumulator.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_americanoption_american_equity_option","label":"American Equity Option","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_americanoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_asianoption_equity_asian_option","label":"Equity Asian Option","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_asianoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
{"id":"docs_userguide_pricing_eq_autodeltahedgedoption_equity_auto_delta_hedged_option","label":"Equity Auto Delta Hedged Option","file_type":"concept","source_file":"Docs/UserGuide/pricing/eq_autodeltahedgedoption.tex","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"The trade is decomposed into realized (historical) hedge P&L, a future-hedge value priced at the hedging volatility on contractual forward dynamics, and an option payoff priced at market volatility/forward curves, because this separates the P&L attributable to the discrete delta-hedging strategy itself (using a fixed hedging vol) from the market-consistent option valuation, allowing both legs to be priced analytically via Black-Scholes."},
